  "notes": "{破|やぶ}く is a transitive verb (⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧). The intransitive pair is ⟦{破|やぶ}れる→破れる：02322_yabureru⟧ (to tear, to be torn).\n\nASPECT (ている):\nThe て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ form indicates ongoing action or a resulting state when combined with other verbs (⟦{紙|かみ}→紙：00712_kami⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{破|やぶ}けて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ uses the intransitive = 'the paper is torn').\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- [object]⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{破|やぶ}く (tear ~)\n- ⟦{紙|かみ}→紙：00712_kami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{破|やぶ}く (tear paper)\n- ⟦{手紙|てがみ}→手紙：00675_tegami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{破|やぶ}く (tear up a letter)\n- ⟦{袋|ふくろ}→袋：00837_fukuro⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{破|やぶ}く (rip open a bag)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {破|やぶ}く vs ⟦{破|やぶ}る→破る：02321_yaburu⟧: Both mean 'to tear,' but ⟦{破|やぶ}る→破る：02321_yaburu⟧ also extends to figurative uses like 'to break (a record)' or 'to defeat.' {破|やぶ}く is primarily for physical tearing.",
